.         
.         
.         * CALCULATING THE MOTHER-FATHER GAP IN I
.         gen DI = abs(I - Idad)
(43,235 missing values generated)

.         
. 
.         
.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * The hypothesis is that couples with daughters will have a smaller "
> mother-father gap" in the time spent on errands, housework, etc. than couples
>  without daughters.
.         * We estimate the following model using OLS:
.         
.         reg DI d_daughter i.numkids, cluster(pid)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =    123,394
                                                F(12, 19315)      =      18.45
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0000
                                                R-squared         =     0.0100
                                                Root MSE          =     5.0712

                               (Std. err. adjusted for 19,316 clusters in pid)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
          DI | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
  d_daughter |   .0043531   .0761299     0.06   0.954    -.1448682    .1535744
             |
     numkids |
          2  |   .3118514   .0699367     4.46   0.000     .1747694    .4489334
          3  |   .9510228   .0965093     9.85   0.000     .7618562    1.140189
          4  |   1.507307   .1534673     9.82   0.000     1.206498    1.808116
          5  |   1.887735   .2849853     6.62   0.000     1.329139    2.446331
          6  |   2.535639   .4927275     5.15   0.000      1.56985    3.501427
          7  |   1.821196   .6015566     3.03   0.002     .6420925    3.000299
          8  |   2.043905   1.503319     1.36   0.174    -.9027309    4.990541
          9  |   3.875843   1.947072     1.99   0.047     .0594121    7.692273
         10  |    4.35379   1.798867     2.42   0.016     .8278545    7.879725
         11  |   4.707238   2.088226     2.25   0.024     .6141346    8.800342
         12  |   6.590571    2.87968     2.29   0.022     .9461478      12.235
             |
       _cons |   4.538409   .0645364    70.32   0.000     4.411912    4.664906
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
.         * As specified in the PAP, the models control for the number of child
> ren 
.         * We also specified a one-sided test  for the coefficient on d_daught
> er in the PAP.
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
.                 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[d_daughter] / _se[d_daughter]

.                 local p_value = ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
